From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: mmc_fdt_parse() never finds mmc-pwrseq for its in-tree callers

mmc_fdt_parse() looks the mmc-pwrseq property up with OF_hasprop(node, ...)
using the node argument raw. All three in-tree callers pass 0:

  sys/arm/allwinner/aw_mmc.c            mmc_fdt_parse(dev, 0, ...)
  sys/arm/broadcom/bcm2835/bcm2835_sdhci.c  mmc_fdt_parse(dev, 0, ...)
  sys/dev/sdhci/sdhci_xenon_fdt.c       mmc_fdt_parse(dev, 0, ...)

so the lookup asks node 0 and mmc-pwrseq is never found, on every one of
them. A node of 0 meaning "use dev's own node" is the convention the other
OFW helpers reached from this same function already follow, and
mmc_fdt_gpio_setup() a little further down this very file has the guard:

	if (node <= 0)
		node = ofw_bus_get_node(dev);

mmc_fdt_parse() is missing it.

It fails silently, which is what makes it worth fixing rather than merely
noting: helper->mmc_pwrseq stays NULL, the host driver skips
MMC_PWRSEQ_SET_POWER() without comment, and a card whose reset line is driven
by mmc-pwrseq is simply left in reset. Nothing is logged.

Found on a BananaPi M64 (aw_mmc with MMCCAM): the AP6212 SDIO WiFi part's
WL_REG_ON on PL2 never rose, so the SDIO probe got no answer to CMD0 and the
card did not enumerate at all.

Add the same guard.

Signed-off-by: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/sys/dev/mmc/mmc_fdt_helpers.c b/sys/dev/mmc/mmc_fdt_helpers.c
index 980785464..af7e481f0 100644
--- a/sys/dev/mmc/mmc_fdt_helpers.c
+++ b/sys/dev/mmc/mmc_fdt_helpers.c
@@ -51,6 +51,23 @@ mmc_fdt_parse(device_t dev, phandle_t node, struct mmc_helper *helper,
 	struct mmc_helper mmc_helper;
 	phandle_t pwrseq_xref;
 
+	/*
+	 * A node of 0 means "use dev's own node" -- the convention every other
+	 * OFW helper called from here already follows (regulator_get_by_ofw_
+	 * property() and gpio_pin_get_by_ofw_property() both accept it). The
+	 * mmc-pwrseq lookup below used `node` raw, so for the three in-tree
+	 * callers that pass 0 -- aw_mmc, bcm2835_sdhci and sdhci_xenon_fdt --
+	 * OF_hasprop() was asking node 0 and mmc-pwrseq was NEVER found. It
+	 * fails silently: helper->mmc_pwrseq stays NULL and the host driver
+	 * simply skips MMC_PWRSEQ_SET_POWER(), so a card whose reset line is
+	 * driven by mmc-pwrseq is left held in reset forever.
+	 *
+	 * Found on a BananaPi M64 (aw_mmc + MMCCAM): the AP6212's WL_REG_ON on
+	 * PL2 never rose, so the SDIO probe got no answer to CMD0.
+	 */
+	if (node <= 0)
+		node = ofw_bus_get_node(dev);
+
 	memset(&mmc_helper, 0, sizeof(mmc_helper));
 	mmc_parse(dev, &mmc_helper, host);
 
